SRC/ls is NOT the source of the ls on this disk==============================================The ls in CMDS/ is GNU fileutils 3.13 built with gcc2, and it reports realpermissions and real timestamps.  The tree in SRC/ls predates three fixes thatbuild needed, so a rebuild from it produces a WORSE ls, not the same one:  1. os9stubs.c's stat() here hardcodes a fixed mode and never sets st_mtime,     so every file would list with invented permissions and a 1969 date.  2. isgraph() is missing.  OS-9's K&R <ctype.h> has every classifier except     that one, and ls.c reaches it through ISGRAPH() in system.h.  3. filemode.c's mode_string() reads Unix octal permission groups     (0700/0070/0007), which do not overlap OS-9's attribute bits     (0x01/0x02/0x04 owner, 0x08/0x10/0x20 public) at all.The three replacement files were not kept.  Rebuilding ls means redoing thatport, not recompiling -- which is why ls is one of the fifteen modules on thisdisk still carrying the original builder's cstart stamp.Everything else under SRC/ does build what CMDS/ ships.